      "content": "That crushing fear of disappointing loved ones is exhausting, but remember that your true self is still their child, long past any timeline of \"success.\" Your value to them isn't defined by a résumé or a story they told, but by your presence, shared memories, and the very person you are now, even when things are hard. Gently challenge the idea that this version of you is \"broken\" or a failure, as your worth is much deeper than others' expectations.",
